Below is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* that fixes the mis‐location of newly created `bpmn:Category`/`bpmn:CategoryValue` when you are working inside a collapsed sub‐process.  In short, we stop pulling “definitions” off the *current* canvas root (which, in a collapsed subprocess, is the plane for that subprocess) and instead grab the *global* definitions from `bpmnjs.getDefinitions()`.

```javascript
### lib/features/modeling/behavior/GroupBehavior.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
  injector.invoke(CommandInterceptor, this);

  /**
   * Gets process definitions
   *
   * @return {ModdleElement} definitions
   */
  function getDefinitions() {
    var rootElement = canvas.getRootElement(),
        businessObject = getBusinessObject(rootElement);

    return businessObject.$parent;
  }
=======
  injector.invoke(CommandInterceptor, this);
  // always grab the global <bpmn:Definitions> via bpmnjs,
  // otherwise collapsed‐subprocesses will become the root
  var bpmnjsInstance = injector.get('bpmnjs');

  /**
   * Gets process definitions
   *
   * @return {ModdleElement} definitions
   */
  function getDefinitions() {
    return bpmnjsInstance.getDefinitions();
  }
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

Explanation:

- The old `getDefinitions()` looked at `canvas.getRootElement()`, which, after drilling into or collapsing a sub‐process, points at the subprocess plane rather than the real `<bpmn:Definitions>`.
- By pulling the true definitions directly from `bpmnjs.getDefinitions()`, any new `Category` / `CategoryValue` now ends up in the real model root and will survive export + re‐import (no more unresolved `<CategoryValue_…>` warnings).
